WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.070
- [Narrator] These nuns
can even break bricks

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:09.930
with their hands

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:13.433
and the purpose behind
this practice is sacred.

00:00:20.439 --> 00:00:24.243
(energetic funk music)

00:00:24.243 --> 00:00:26.910
(playful music)

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:36.790
The Drukpa Order is a branch of Buddhism

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:39.140
that has been around
for thousands of years

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:42.410
but in 2008, the nunnery
based in Katmandu, Nepal

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:43.850
started to learn Kung Fu

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:45.963
as part of their spiritual practice.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.333
Jigme wanted to be a nun
since she was a little girl.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:03.245
No other nunnery in Nepal
does Kung Fu training

00:01:03.245 --> 00:01:04.670
(nuns yelling in unison)

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:07.330
and Jigme and her
sisters go the extra mile

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:08.893
to master this art form.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:19.080
They run and climb up stairs
to strengthen their bodies

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:20.760
and they used sticks and fans

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.263
to enhance their coordination.

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:27.350
And the purpose of training
these nuns to fight

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:30.553
all comes back to the philosophies
of peace and equality.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.910
The nuns also take these philosophies

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:43.610
and apply them to disadvantaged
communities in Nepal.

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:47.540
In 2015 when a devastating
earthquake hit Katmandu,

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.963
the nuns knew this was
their call to action.

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:09.720
The nuns also biked 14,000
miles throughout Nepal

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:12.993
to protest against the human
trafficking of women and girls.

